        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: സൽക്കാരം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സൽക്കാരം — salkkāraṁ — \"a banquet\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മാനേജർ ജീവനക്കാർക്ക് ഒരു സൽക്കാരം നടത്തി. mānējar jīvanakkārkkŭ oru salkkāraṁ naṭatti. The manager held a banquet for the staff."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A banquet is held: സൽക്കാരം (salkkāraṁ) നടത്തുക."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സൽക്കാരം (salkkāraṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit satkāra, \"kind treatment, hospitality\" (CDIAL 13108), from sat, \"good\", and kāra, \"a doing\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
